{"id": "EUVD-2026-97068", "enisaUuid": "41579589-a980-391d-8138-12b2543e4e7a", "description": "pH7Builder (pH7 Social Dating CMS) before 18.6.0 contains a hard-coded API key vulnerability in Tool.class.php that allows unauthenticated attackers to bypass API access checks by spoofing the Host header. Attackers can send Host: localhost with private_api_key=dev772277 and the default allowed URL to retrieve member emails, IP addresses, phone numbers, and bank account fields.", "datePublished": "2026-10-11T14:58:06", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-13T19:19:00", "baseScore": 8.7, "baseScoreVersion": "4.0", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:4.0/AV:N/AC:L/AT:N/PR:N/UI:N/VC:H/VI:N/VA:N/SC:N/SI:N/SA:N", "references": ["https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS/commit/cfe1e0c418946b868db8c399d0cf6b122552efd2", "https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS/blob/v18.5.1/_protected/framework/Api/Tool.class.php#L25-L48", "https://github.com/pH7Software/pH7-Social-Dating-CMS", "https://www.vulncheck.com/advisories/ph7builder-before-18.6.0-hard-coded-api-key-bypass-via-host-header"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-108905", "GHSA-jfr6-f5qc-qp53"], "assigner": "VulnCheck", "epss": 0.31, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "07e33091-71ae-3866-b591-6ad46a96fbb7", "product": {"name": "ph7builder", "vendor": {"name": "ph7software"}}, "product_version": "0 <18.6.0"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "867483e2-546e-31f3-9701-d82c48c3888b", "vendor": {"name": "ph7software"}}], "isExploited": false}